// Defect-seeded mutation campaign.
//
// WHY THIS EXISTS.  Hand-designed matrices saturate: once a dimension is
// enumerated, more cases buy nothing, and the project's own record shows the
// big campaigns found nothing while a new oracle found two defects.  The
// complementary axis is *neighbourhood*: start from a minimal witness that is
// already known to break the compiler and mutate it, so the search spends its
// budget where the compiler is demonstrably fragile.
//
// The validity gate is the whole trick: only a `judge` Defect finding counts.
// A mutation that merely fails to parse is an invalid experiment, not a
// finding, so byte-level mutation cannot manufacture "new bugs".

import {
  "moonbitlang/core/async",
  "moonbitlang/core/env",
  "moonbitlang/x/fs",
  "I3eg1nner/mbtfuzz/mutate",
  "I3eg1nner/mbtfuzz/stager",
}

options(
  "allow-experimental-packages": [ "moonbitlang/core/async" ],
)

pkgtype(kind: "executable")
